Subject: [PATCH 3/3] imgui: never pass a runtime string as a printf format

ImGui::Text and friends are printf-style. Passing a std::string straight in as
the format means any '%' inside it is interpreted - and these strings are BYML
keys, actor display names and template titles, i.e. game data and user input.
A name containing "%s" reads a garbage pointer off the stack.

Use TextUnformatted for plain strings, and an explicit "%s" for TextColored,
which has no unformatted variant. This is also what Arch's default
-Werror=format-security catches, so the package will not build without it.

